 553.78 \n Bengal \n TOTAL : 182 273 98 553 271983.78 64346.21 65544.26 129890.47 142093.31 21716.83 4742.01 3696.99 8439.01 13277.82 \n \n\n 271 \nNational river interlinking project \n†838. SHRI PRABHAT JHA: Will the Minister of WATER RESOURCES be \npleased to state: \n(a) the present Status of the 'National River Interlinking Project' \nlaunched during the NDA regime; \n(b) the details of allocation of budget for this project made by the \nNDA Government and the present Government; \n(c) whether Government believe that the National calamity such as \nflood and drought could be avoided through this project; and \n(d) if so, the details of the steps taken by Government for this \nproject during the last five years? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRIMATI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a), (c) and (d) The Ministry of Water Resources \n(MOWR) (erstwhile Ministry of Irrigation) and Central Water Commission \n(CWC) formulated a National Perspective Plan (NPP) for Water Resources \nDevelopment in 1980 envisaging inter-basin transfer of water from surplus \nbasins to deficit basins/areas which comprises of two components, namely. \nHimalayan Rivers Development Component and Peninsular Rivers Development \nComponent. National Water Development Agency (NWDA) was set up under the \nMOWR in 1982 for carrying out various technical studies to establish the \nfeasibility of the proposals of NPP and to give conc rete shape to it. \nBased on various studies conducted, NWDA has identified 30 links. (16 \nunder Peninsular Component & 14 under Himalayan Component) for \npreparation of Feasibility Reports (FRs). Out of these, FRs of 14 links \nunder Peninsular Component and 2 links (Indian Portion) under Himalayan \nComponent have already been completed. \nThe Inter-linking proposals under NPP envisages additional benefits of \n25 million ha. of irrigation from surface water, 10 million ha. by \nincreased use of ground waters and generation of 34 Thousand MW of power \napart from the incidental benefits of flood moderation, navigation, water \nsupply, salinity & pollution control etc. \nAs per National Common Minimum Programme (NCMP) of the Government \ninterlinking of rivers (ILR) programme is being pursued with focus on \npeninsular component and five peninsular links have been identified as \npriority links for consensus building between the concerned States. The \nconsensus group headed by Chairman, Central Water Commission (CWC) has \nheld seven meetings during last five years, one for Ken -  Betwa link, \nthree for Parbati - Kalisindh - Chambal link, one for Godavari \n(Polavaram) – Krishna (Vijayawada) link and two for Par – Tapi – Narmada \n& Damanganga –  Pinjal links together. A tripartite Memorandum of \nUnderstanding was signed between the Union Minister of Water Resources \nand Chief Ministers of the Government of Madhya Pradesh and the \nGovernment of Uttar Pradesh on 25.8.2005 for preparation of Detailed \nProject Report (DPR) of one of the priority link namely Ken- Betwa. NWDA \nhas completed its DPR in December, 2008. Further the Government of \n\n 272 \nMaharashtra & Gujarat also conveyed their concurrence for preparation of \nDPRs of Par - Tapi - Narmada & Damanganga -  Pinjal links and NWDA has \ntaken up their DPRs which are planned to be completed by December, 2011. \n(b) Depending upon the requirement, the Grant- in-aid released to NWDA \nduring the period of NDA Government & Present Government are given below: \n†Original notice of the question was received  in Hindi. \n\n 273 \n  Rs. Crore \n(i) NDA Government (1999-2000 to 2003-04) 73.23 \n(ii) Present Government (2004-2005 to 2008-2009  (up to 31st January 2009)\n 106.41 \nProtection of natural sources of water in Uttarakhand \n†839. SHRI BHAGAT SINGH KOSHYARI: Will the Minister of WATER \nRESOURCES be pleased to state: \n(a) whether Government has made any scheme for the protection and \npromotion of constantly decreasing natural sources of water in \nUttarakhand; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRIMATI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) to (c) The State Government of Uttarakhand is \nimplementing a World Bank aided \"Uttarakhand Decentralised Watershed \nDevelopment Project\" costing Rs. 402 crore in 76 selected micro-\nwatersheds of 11 districts since September, 2004 for protection of water \nresources of the State and to promote natural water sources. \nIrrigation projects in West Bengal \n840. SHRI R.C. SINGH: Will the Minister of WATER RESOURCES be pleased \nto state: \n(a) the details of medium irrigation projects, out of the total 221 \nprojects as per the Tenth Plan undertaken in West Bengal in the Tenth \nPlan; \n(b) the details of medium irrigation projects proposed to be \nundertaken in the Eleventh Plan; \n(c) the amount that has been allotted and released for the above \nprojects in the Tenth Plan and the Eleventh Plan; \n(d) whether it is a fact that many medium projects are delayed due to \nnon-release of money by his Ministry; and \n(e) if so, the reasons therefor? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRIMATI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) As per information available in Central Water \nCommission, nine medium irrigation projects in West Bengal were ongoing \nduring X Plan and eight of them have spilled over to XI Plan. The details \nof these projects are given in Statement-I (See below). \n(b) In addition to above eight medium projects which spilled over from \nX Plan, twelve new medium irrigation projects are proposed to be taken up \nduring XI Plan in the S tate of West Bengal. The details of these twelve \nnew medium projects are given in Statement-II (See below). \n(c) to (e) Irrigation is a State subject and the projects are planned, \nfunded and implemented by the concerned S tate Governments from their own \nresources as per their own priorities. Central Government provides \nfinancial assistance to the State Government under the Accelerated \n\n 274 \nIrrigation Benefits Programme for expeditious completion of ongoing \nprojects as per the guidelines of the programme in force from time to \ntime. \nThe details of CLA/Grant released for medium irrigation projects of \nWest Bengal during X Plan and XI Plan are given in Statement-III. \n†Original notice of the question was received  in Hindi. \n\n 275 \nStatement-I \nThe details of physical and financial details of ongoing medium irrigation projects of XI plan in the State of West \nBengal \n        (Rs. in Crore)     (Pot. In Th. \nHa.) \nSl. Name of  Basin /River District Plan Approval           Estimated  cost Cum. Antici- Antici- Outlay Ultimate Pot. Antici-\n Antici- \n projects  benefitted of Status   Exp.   pated pated proposed Poten- Created pated pated \n    Start    upto during Exp. by Sub tial upto created Created \n      Original Latest end of X  upto group  end during upto  \n        IX Plan Plan end in   of IX X end \n        (3/02)  of X XI  Plan Plan of X \n          Plan Plan  (3/2002)  Plan \n               (3/2007) \n1. Golamarajore Ganga/  Purulia V 1976/PC 0.5200 3.9220 3.0600 0.1645 3.2245 0.6955 0.9800 0.2600 0.5000 0.7600 \n  Kangsabati   \n2. Moutorejore Ganga/ Purulia V 1974/PC 0.4000 1.8970 0.6400 0.0576 0.6976 1.2024 1.0780 0.5740 0.5020 1.0760 \n  Kangsabati   \n3. Hanumata C Ganga/ Purulia VII 1975/PC 0.8300 8.9669 5.5800 0.4513 6.0313 2.7687 2.7660 1.7380 0.9630 2.7010 \n  Kangsabati  \n4. Tatko Ganga/ Purulia V 1975/PC 0.9800 16.6063 7.7800 0.5768 8.3568 4.2132 2.4940 1.4540 0.3660 1.8200 \n  Kangsabati  \n5. Patloi Ganga/ Purulia V 1975/PC 0.9000 13.3413 5.5200 0.8662 6.3862 4.4138 2.1580 0.0000 0.1700 0.1700 \n  Kangsabati  \n6. Beko Ganga/ Purulia V 1975/PC 0.6400 5.9000 4.1900 0.2516 4.4416 1.4584 1.5860 1.0020 0.5050 1.5070 \n  Kangsabati  \n7. Khaira Bera Ganga/ Purulia VII 1988/PC 1.1000 4.1500 3.1900 0.2296 3.4196 0.7304 1