08.15 1.84 4144.16 \n16 Manipur 155.00 24.00 6.50 13.54 199.04 \n\n 300 \n1 2 3 4 5 6 7 \n17 Meghalaya 0.30 22.00 0.35 2.50 25.15 \n18 Mizoram 0.01 34.53 0.20 0.00 34.74 \n19 Nagaland 0.00 47.66 1.00 1.50 50.16 \n20 Orissa 657.90 98.20 11.00 17.50 784.60 \n21 Punjab 337.47 149.05 80.00 83.48 650.00 \n22 Rajasthan 974.44 169.81 67.60 8.08 1219.93 \n23 Sikkim 0.00 7.50 0.25 6.60 14.35 \n24 Tamil Nadu 389.12 111.10 22.75 43.00 565.97 \n25 Tripura 16.45 31.30 0.50 15.01 63.26 \n26 Uttar Pradesh* 1824.73 321.30 176.15 40.00 2362.18 \n27 Uttaranchal 96.39 23.92 3.50 12.06 135.87 \n28 West Bengal 158.97 64.00 10.31 140.78 374.06 \n Total States 29397.59 5336.72 1778.88 1379.67 37892.86 \n Union Territories \n29 A & N Island 0.00 7.15 0.00 8.05 15.20 \n30 Chandigarh* 0.00 0.65 0.00 0.00 0.65 \n31 D & N Haveli* 0.00 3.11 2.30 1.00 6.41 \n32 Daman & Diu 0.10 0.15 0.00 0.39 0.64 \n33 Delhi 0.00 20.00 0.00 49.00 69.00 \n34 Lakshadweep 0.00 0.00 0.00 6.03 6.03 \n35 Pondicherry 0.00 16.17 0.00 23.29 39.46 \n Total U.Ts. 0.10 47.23 2.30 87.76 137.39 \n Total States & U.Ts.29397.69 5383.95 1781.18 1467.43 38030.25 \n Central Sector 132.50 67.50 300.00 100.00 600.00 \n Grand Total 29530.19 5451.45 2081.18 1567.43 38630.25 \n* Proposed outlay by the State; approved outlay yet to be finalised \nPower project at Indo-Bhutan border \n848. SHRI BISWAJIT DAIMARY: Will the Minister of WATER RESOURCES be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether Government is aware that after completion of the power \nprojects at Bhutan, the Indo- Bhutan Border especially Bodoland \nTerritorial Autonomous District (BTAD) in Assam is suffering continuous \n\n 301 \nflood/erosion; \n\n 302 \n(b) if so, the measures taken in this regard; \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor; \n(d) the details of the agreement draft, if any, made between India and \nBhutan for setting up of hydro-power plants at Bhutan; \n(e) whether Government has taken any permanent initiative or measures \nto protect flood or erosion in BTAD; \n(f) if so, the details thereof; \n(g) the rivers which have their plain source in Bhutan; and \n(h) the rivers on which the power plants have been set up and the \nnames of the power plants? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) to (c) There were some press reports in Assam \nduring 2007 that the Hydropower Projects in Bhutan are causing floods in \nthe region. Subsequently, Government of Assam also raised the concern on \nthe issue. Accordingly, the issue was discussed with the concerned \nBhutanese authorities during the 2nd meeting of Joint Group of Experts on \nFlood Management between India and Bhutan. Following such discussions, it \nhas been found that the Hydropower Projects in Bhutan are not directly \nresponsible for the floods/ erosion in Assam. \n(d) In July 2006, an agreement was signed between Government of India \nand Royal Government of Bhutan on cooperation in Hydropower sector by \nwhich Government of India (GoI) agreed to import 5000 MW of hydropower \nfrom Royal Government of Bhutan (RGoB) by 2020. During the visit of \nHon'ble Prime Minister of India to Bhutan in May 2008, this target was \nsubsequently revised to 10,000 MW. In July 2007, India and Bhutan signed \nan agreement to implement the 1095 MW Punatsangchu- 1 Hydroelectric \nProject. Earlier in 1994, an Inter- Government Agreement between GoI and \nRGoB was signed on the Tala and Kurichu Hydroelectric Projects for loan \nrepayment and tariff fixation. Protocols to the Inter-  Government \nAgreement on the Tala and Kurichu Hydroelectric Projects respectively, \nwere signed in 2008. \n(e) and (f) In order to formulate the flood forecasts on transboarder \nrivers originating from Bhutan, a scheme titled \"Comprehensive Scheme for \nEstablishment of Hydro- meteorological and Flood Forecasting Network on \nrivers common to India and Bhutan\" is in operation. The network consists \nof 35 hydro-meteorological/ meteorological stations located in Bhutan and \n\n 303 \nis being maintained by the Royal Government of Bhutan with funding from \nIndia. The data received from these stations are utilized in India by the \nCentral Water Commission for formulating flood forecasts. A Joint Expert \nTeam (JET) consisting of officials from the Government of India and Royal \nGovernment of Bhutan continuously reviews the progress and other \nrequirements of the scheme. \nThe matter relating to the problem of floods caused by the rivers \noriginating from Bhutan and coming to India are discussed in a Joint \nGroup of Experts (JGE) on Flood Management  constituted  \n\n 304 \nbetween India and Bhutan to discuss and assess the probable causes and \neffects of the recurring floods and erosion in the southern foothills of \nBhutan and adjoining plains in India and recommend to both Governments \nappropriate and mutually acceptable remedial measures. Two meetings of \nJGE have been held between India and Bhutan so far. \nFurther, Bodoland Territorial Council (BTC) has informed that they \nhave currently taken up 10 number of schemes with a total estimated cost \nof Rs.97.42 crores to protect Bodoland area from flood and erosion. \n(g) The major rivers entering into India from Bhutan are Sankosh, \nManas, Jaldhaka, Torsa, Wangchu, Gaurang, Pagladiya, Beki and Dhansiri. \n(h) The names of the rivers alongwith the power plants that have been \nset up through Government of India's cooperation are as below: \nRiver Hydroelectric Project \nWangchu i) Chukha Hydro-electric project \n ii) Tala Hydro-electric project \nKurichu Kurichhu Hydro-electric project \n(Tributary of river Manas) \nPunatsangchhu Punatsangchhu-I (Under Construction) \n(Tributary of river Sonkosh) \nRepairing of breach of Kosi river \n†849. SHRI SHIVANAND TIWARI: \n SHRI RAM JETHMALANI: \nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES be pleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact that the breach in Kosi river that occurred \nlast August has been repaired and now Kosi would take its old course; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether Government has formulated any scheme to put to use the \nforceful flow of this river; \n(d) if so, the outline of the scheme; \n(e) whether Government of Nepal's consent is also being sought in this \nregard; and \n(f) if so, the details thereof? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) Yes, Sir. The breach has been repaired and \nriver Kosi is now flowing along its original course through the Kosi \n\n 305 \nbarrage. \n†Original notice of the question was received  in Hindi. \n\n 306 \n(b) The breach section has been closed and raised upto a level of \n82.50 m in the first phase of work on 16.2.2009. Earthwork in the \nembankment to raise it further upto 87.25m is in progress. \n(c) to (f) 269 m High Dam has been envisaged on river Kosi at \nBarahkshetra (Nepal) to utilise the Kosi water for hydropower generation \nand to improve the irrigation water supplies besides flood mitigation in \nNorth Bihar. To prepare the Detailed Project Report (DPR) of Saptakosi \nHigh Dam Project, a Joint Project Office (JPO) has been set up jointly at \nBiratnagar (Nepal) in August 2004 to undertake the field investigation \nand formulation of the scheme jointly with Nepal. \nSardar Sarovar Yojana \n†850. SHRI SHREEGOPAL VYAS: Will the Minister of WATER RESOURCES \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) whether any initiative is being taken to revive the Sardar Sarovar \nYojana; \n(b) whether any discussion has been held about needs and provisions of \nresettlement; and \n(c) the role of Central Government regarding above mentioned subject? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) Sardar Sarovar Project is an on going Project \nbeing implemented by the four party State Governments of Gujarat, Madhya \nPradesh, Maharashtra and Rajasthan in accordance with Narmada Water \nDisputes Tribunal Award. \n(b) The Narmada Water Disputes Tribunal (NWDT) Award stipulated \nprovisions of Resettlement & Rehabilitation of Project Affected Persons. \nThe implementation of provisions of Resettlement & Rehabilitation (R&R) \nis being monitored by Narmada Control Authority and its R&R Sub- Group on \na regular basis. \n(c) In accordance with the directions of Narmada Water Disputes \nTribunal Award, the Central Government has formulated Narmada Water \nScheme under Section- 6(A) of Inter- State Water Dispute Act, 1956 and  \ninter-alia, constituted the Narmada Control Authority, Sardar Sarovar \nConstruction Advisory Committee and Review Committee of Narmada Control \nAuthority for implementation of Sardar Sarovar Project. This is as per \ndirections of NWDT Award, Environmental Clearance Order of Ministry of \nEnvironment & Forests and various directions of the Hon'ble Supreme Court \nand Hon'ble High Courts. \n\n 307 \nBrahmaputra Board \n851. SHRI BIRENDRA PRASAD BAISHYA: Will the Minister of WATER RESOURCES \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) whether the plan to restructure Brahmaputra Board has been \nimplemented by Government; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n†Original notice of the question was received  in Hindi. \n\n 308 \n(c) the manpower and institutional break up finalized as well as \nadditional power or autonomy granted to upgrade the board to an effective \nfunctional entity; and \n(d) if not, the reasons for delay and by when it is likely to be \nrestructured? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) No, Sir. \n(b) and (c) Do not arise. \n(d) Proposal for restructuring of Brahmaputra Board by way of \namendment of Brahmaputa Board Act, 1980 is being finalized in \nconsultation with the concerned Central Government Ministries/Departments \nand the State Governments which is a time consuming process. After \nfinalization of the proposal, a bill seeking amendment of the Act will be \nbrought up before the Parliament. Subsequently, the amended Act will be \nnotified in the official Gazette and the Board will be restructured \naccordingly. The restructuring of the Board will depend on the final \npassing of the Bill by the Parliament. \nWater dispute of Mhadei river \n852. SHRI SHANTARAM LAXMAN NAIK: Will the Minister of WATER RESOURCES \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) whether there is a Mhadei River water dispute between the State of \nGoa and the State of Karnataka; \n(b) contentions in brief of both the States; \n(c) steps taken by the Government in this regard; \n(d) whether a delegation, led by the Chief Minister of Goa met the \nPrime Minister of India, recently; and \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) to (e) The Government of Karnataka in April, \n2002 requested for clearance of proposal from inter- State angle for \ndiversion of 7.56 TMC of water from Mahadayi basin to Malaprabha basin \nthrough implementation of Kalasa and Bhandurinalla schemes to meet the \ndrinking water needs of Hubli/Dharwad cities. The Ministry of Water \nResources (MOWR) gave and 'in principle' clearance to the proposal to \nmeet the drinking water need of Hubli/Dharwad from water availability \nangle on 30th April, 2002. The Government of Goa in July, 2002 took \nstrong exception to the grant of this clearance by the Ministry and \nrequested for setting up of an Inter- State Water Disputes Tribunal under \n\n 309 \nthe Inter-State Water Disputes Act, 1956 for resolution of the dispute. \nIn view of this, the 'in-principle' clearance grantee by the Ministry was \nplaced 'in abeyance' in September, 2002 with a view to resolve the matter \nby an agreement between the two States, failing which by an award of the \nTribunal. Later, a view emerged in the MOWR that he said dispute cannot \nbe settled by Negotiations. \n\n 310 \nA delegation, led by the Chief Minister of Goa, met the Prime Minister \nof India on 7.1.2009 and submitted a memorandum to take immediate action \nto stop Karnataka from proceeding with construction of Disputed Projects \nfor diversion of water from water deficient Mandovi (Mahadayi) basin to \nwater surplus Malaprabha basin and constitute the tribunal immediately as \nper the request of Goa dated 09.07.2002. \nMeanwhile, the Government of Goa filed a suit in the Supreme Court for \nsetting up of Water Disputes Tribunal for adjudication of the above river \nwater dispute and an Interlocutory Application (IA) for stay in \nconstruction activities by Karnataka in September 2006. The court in the \nhearing dated 30.4.2008 ordered that as per the statement made by the \nState of Karnataka in i ts counter affidavit filed on 27th September, \n2006, the State of Karnataka will not actually utilize the waters or \ndivert the waters under the Kalasa Bhanduri project till next date of \nhearing. \nInterlinking of 30 rivers \n†853. SHRI RAJ MOHINDER SINGH MAJITHA: \n SHRI SHIVANAND TIWARI: \nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES be pleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact that National Water Development Agency has \nsanctioned the projects of interlinking of 30 rivers of the country; \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the time when this sanction was \ngiven; \n(c) whether the construction works on these sanctioned projects has \nstarted; and \n(d) if so, the river projects on which construction works have started \nand the total amount spent on these projects till December, 2008? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) to (d) National Water Development Agency \n(NWDA) has identified 30 links (16 under Peninsular Component & 14 under \nHimalayan Component) for preparation of Feasibility Reports (FRs) under \nNational Perspective Plan (NPP). The names of these links are given in \nthe Statement (See below). Out of these, FRs of 14 links under Peninsular \nComponent and of 2 links (Indian Portion) under Himalayan Component have \nbeen completed. Detailed Project Report (DPR) of one priority link namely \nKen - Betwa has also been completed . Further, NWDA has taken up the DPRs \nof another two priority links namely Par -  Tapi - Narmada & Damanganga - \nPinjal which are planned to be completed by December, 2011. \nAt present, no interlinking project under NPP is under implementation. \nTheir implementation depends upon the consensus and cooperation of the \n\n 311 \nconcerned states and agreement with the neighboring countries. \nNWDA has incurred an expenditure of Rs. 244.84 crore upto December, \n2008 for preparation of Pre- Feasibility Reports (PFRs)/FRs/DPRs of river \nlink proposals under NPP, preparation of PFRs/FRs of intra S tate links \nand other studies in this regard. \n†Original notice of the question was received  in Hindi. \n\n 312 \nStatement \nDetails of name of water transfer links indetified under national \nperspective plan \nPeninsular Rivers Development Component \n1. Mahanadi (Manibhadra) - Godavari (Dowlaiswaram) link \n2. Godavari (Polavaram) - Krishna (Vijayawada) link* \n3. Godavari (Inchampalli) - Krishna (Pulichintala) link \n4. Godavari (Inchampalli) - Krishna (Nagarjunasagar) link \n5. Krishna (Nagarjunasagar) - Pennar (Somasila) link \n6. Krishna (Srisailam) - Pennar link \n7. Krishna (Almatti) - Pennar link \n8. Pennar (Somasila) - Cauvery (Grand Anicut) link \n9. Cauvery (Kattalai) - Vaigai - Gundar link \n10. Parbati - Kalisindh - Chambal link* \n11. Damanganga - Pinjal link* \n12. Par - Tapi - Narmada link* \n13. Ken - Betwa link* \n14. Pamba - Achankovil - Vaippar link* \n15. Netravati - Hemavati Link \n16. Bedti - Varda link \nHimalayan Rivers Development Component \n1. Kosi-Mechi link \n2. Kosi-Ghaghra link \n3. Gandak-Ganga link \n4. Ghaghra-Yamuna link \n5. Sarda-Yamuna link \n6. Yamuna-Rajasthan link \n7. Rajasthan-Sabarmati link \n8. Chunar-Sone Barrage link \n9. Sone Dam - Southern Tributaries of Ganga link \n10. Manas-Sankosh-Tista-Ganga (M-S-T-G) link \n11. Jogighopa-Tista-Farakka (Alternate to M-S-T-G) link \n12. Farakka-Sunderbans link \n13. Ganga-Damodar- Subernarekha link \n14. Subernarekha-Mahanadi link \n* Priority links \n\n 313 \nCharge for use of underground water \n854. SHRI NANDI YELLAIAH: Will the Minister of WATER RESOURCES be \npleased to state: \n(a) the rates being charged from Andhra Pradesh vis-a-vis other States \nfor the use of under ground water for agricultural purposes; \n(b) the reasons for variance in rates prescribed for various States \nand the norms for fixing these rates; \n(c) the main recommendations of the expert committee set up by \nGovernment to rationalize these rates; and \n(d) the details of action taken on these recommendation by Government? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) and (b) The rates for use of ground water for \nagricultural purposes are decided by the State Governments. As per report \nreceived from Andhra Pradesh Government, the use of ground water for \nagriculture purposes is not being charged. \n(c) and (d) Ministry of Water Resources has not constituted any expert \ncommittee for examining rationalization of rates for the use of ground \nwater for agriculture purposes. \nDeclaration of rivers as national assets \n855. DR. JANARDHAN WAGHMARE: \n SHRIMATI SHOBHANA BHARTIA: \nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES be pleased to state: \n(a) whether to increase irrigation potential and harness the hydro-\npower possibilities, the Central Government had decided to adopt some \nrivers as \"National Assets'; \n(b) if so, the details of rivers in the country which have been \nadopted by the Central Government so far; \n(c) whether Government is aware that water dispute amongst some States \nhave created imbalance in increasing irrigation potential; and \n(d) if so, the strategies Government propose to formulate to have a \nproper control of various rivers? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) In order to increase irrigated area in the \ncountry and to harness hydropower potential, the Central Government has \ndeclared 14 water resources projects as 'National Projects'. \n\n 314 \n(b) The details of the projects declared as National Projects with \nriver/river basin in which these projects are located is given in the \nStatement (See below). \n(c) and (d) Most of the major rivers in India are inter- State in \ncharacter having catchments/watersheds in two or more States. The water \ndisputes arise amongst the basin States  \n\n 315 \nwith regard to the use, distribution or control of the waters in respect \nof these inter-State rivers/river valleys. \nThe settlement of disputes by negotiations foster a spirit of \ninvolvement of the States concerned and ultimately lead to more \nexpeditious development of water resources. Success has been achieved in \nresolving the disputes by negotiations in the past and about 125 \nagreements have been reached between the basin States. \nThe Government of India has enacted the Inter-  State Water Disputes \nAct, 1956 for adjudication of disputes relating to waters of inter -State \nrivers and river valley. When the Central Government is satisfied that \nthe dispute cannot be settled by negotiations, the same is referred to a \ntribunal under the provisions of Inter State River Water Disputes (ISRWD) \nAct, 1956. At present, three Tribunals have been constituted in respect \nof water disputes related to Ravi & Beas, Cauvery and Krishna river under \nISRWD Act 1956. \nFurther, the Government of India enacted the River Boards Act 1956 \nunder entry 56. The River Boards Act envisages setting up of River Boards \nfor Inter-State river basins to advise the State Governments in planning \nand development of inter S tate rivers. So far, no river board has been \nestablished under this act. However, some River Boards, Commissions, \nAuthorities have been constituted through Government resolution, \nexecutive orders or Acts based upon interstate agreements, S tate \nreorganization acts and award of tribunal such as Betwa River Board, \nBansagar Control Board, Tungabhadra Board, Narmada Control Authority, \nBhakra Beas Management Board and Upper Yamuna River Board. \nStatement \nList of projects declared as national projects by Government \nSl.No. Name of the Project State \n1 Teesta Barrage West Bengal \n2 Shahpur Kandi Punjab \n3 Bursar J & K \n4 2nd Ravi Vyas Link Punjab \n5 Ujh multipurpose project J & K \n6 Gyspa project HP \n7 Lakhvar Vyasi Uttaranchal \n8 Kishau HP/Uttaranchal \n9 Renuka HP \n10 Noa-Dehang Dam Project Arunanchal Pradesh \n11 Kulsa Dam Project Assam \n12 Upper Siang Arunanchal Pradesh \n\n 316 \n13 Gosikhurd Maharashtra \n14 Ken Betwa Madhya Pradesh, Uttar \n    Pradesh \n\n 317 \n12.00 NOON \nScarcity of water \n†856. DR. MURLI MANOHAR JOSHI: \n SHRI RAM JETHMALANI: \nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES be pleased to state: \n(a) whether Government has taken notice of the report published by \nworld Economic Forum on water; \n(b) if so, whether it has sounded of serious warning about scarcity of \nwater; \n(c) if so, what is Government's reaction thereto; \n(d) whether it is also a fact that shortage in country's availability \nof water has been estimated during the past one decade; and \n(e) if so, the extent of this shortage and average annual availability \nof water at present in the country? \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES (SHRI JAY \nPRAKASH NARAYAN YADAV): (a) to (c) The World Economic Forum has drafted a \nReport titled \" The Bubble is Close to Bursting: A Forecast of the Main \nEconomic and Geopolitical Water Issues Likely to Arise in the World \nduring the Next Two Decades\" for discussion at the Forum Annual Meeting \n2009. Various challenges related to water including the aspects of \nscarcity of water in respect of Food and Agriculture, Energy, Trade, \nNational Economic Security, Cities, People without Water and Sanitation, \nGlobal Business and The Financial Sector have been highlighted and action \npoint identified in the draft Report. Most of the issues are duly \nreflected in the National Water Policy and several initiatives have also \nbeen taken by respective State Governments and Government of India. \n(d) and (e) The availability of the water in the country has been \nassessed from time to time. The overall annual water availability of \nIndia has been assessed as about 1869 Billion Cubic Meter (BCM). No \ndecline in the overall annual water availability has been observed in the \ncountry. \n_____ \n(MR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN in the Chair) \nPAPERS LAID ON THE TABLE \nReports and Accounts (2007-08) of the Water and Power Consultancy \nServices (India) Limited, New Delhi and Related Papers \n जल संसाधन मंत्रालय म� राज्य मंत्री (श्री जय प्रकाश नारायण यादव): महोदय, म� �नम्न�ल�खत \n\n 318 \nपत्र सभा पटल पर रखता हूं:- \n I. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers, under \nsub-section (1) of Section 619A of the Companies Act, 1956: \n†Original notice of the question was received  in Hindi. \n\n 319 \n  (a) Thirty-ninth Annual Report and Accounts of the Water and \nPower Consultancy Services (India) Limited, formerly known \nas WAPCOS, New Delhi, for the year 2007- 2008, together with \nthe Auditor's Report on the Accounts and the comments of the \nComptroller and Auditor General of India thereon. \n  (b) Statement by Government accepting the above Report. \n II. Statement (in English and Hindi) giving reasons for the delay in \nlaying the papers mentioned at (I) above. [Placed in Library. See \nNo. L.T. 10719/09] \nReports and Accounts of various Hotel Management Institutes, Akademies, \nCultural Institutes and Science Museums (2006-07, 2007-08) and Related \nPapers \n THE MINISTER OF TOURISM AND MINISTER OF CULTURE (SHRIMATI AMBIKA SON): \nSir, I beg to lay on the Table, a copy each (in English and Hindi) of the \nfollowing papers: \n (i) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the National Council for Hotel \nManagement and Catering Technology (NCHMCT), NOIDA, for the \nyear 2007-2008. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Council. \n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10773/09] \n (ii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the National Council for Hotel \nManagement and Catering Technology and Applied Nutrition \n(NCHMCT), Srinagar, for the year 2007-2008. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Society. \n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10589/09] \n (iii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Lalit Kala Akademi, New \nDelhi, for the year 2007 -2008, together with the Auditor's \nReport on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Akademi. \n  (c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers \nmentioned at (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. \n10777/09] \n (iv) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the West Zone Cultural Centre \n(WZCC), Udaipur, for the year 2007- 2008, together with the \nAuditor's Report on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Centre. \n  (c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers \n\n 320 \nmentioned at (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. \n10776/09] \n (v) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the South Central Zone \nCultural Centre (SCZCC), Nagpur, for the year 2007- 2008, \ntogether with the Auditor's Report on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Centre. \n\n 321 \n  (c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers \nmentioned at (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. \n10774/09] \n (vi) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Eastern Zone Cultural \nCentre (EZCC), Kolkata, for the year 2007- 2008, together \nwith the Auditor's Report on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Centre. \n  (c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers \nmentioned at (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. \n10775/09] \n (vii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Sahitya Akademi, New \nDelhi, for the year 2007 -2008, together with the Auditor's \nReport on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Akademi. \n  (c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers \nmentioned at (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. \n10591/09] \n (viii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the North Central Zone \nCultural Centre (NCZCC), Allahabad, for the year 2007- 2008, \ntogether with the Auditor's Report on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Centre. \n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10593/09] \n (ix) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Kalakshetra Foundation, \nChennai, for the year 2007-2008, together with the Auditor's \nReport on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Foundation. \n  (c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers \nmentioned at (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. \n10590/09] \n (x) (a) Annual Report of the National Council of Science Museums \n(NCSM), Kolkata, for the year 2006-2007. \n  (b) Annual Accounts of the National Council of Science Museums \n(NCSM), Kolkata, for the year 2006-2007 and the Audit Report \nthereon. \n  (c) Review by Government on the working of the above Council. \n  (d) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers \nmentioned at (a) and (b) above. [Placed in Library. See No. \n\n 322 \nL.T. 10592/09] \n (xi) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Victoria Memorial Hall, \nKolkata, for the year 2006-2007, together with the Auditor's \nReport on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Hall. \n  (c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers \nmentioned at (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. \n10587/09] \n\n 323 \n (xii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the North Zone Cultural Centre \n(NZCC), Patiala, for the year 2007- 2008, together with the \nAuditor's Report on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Centre. \n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10588/09] \n (xiii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Centre for Cultural \nResources and Training, New Delhi, for the year 2007- 2008, \ntogether with the Auditor's Report on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Centre. \n  (c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers \nmentioned at (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. \n10772/09] \n__________ \nNotifications of Ministry of Civil Aviations \n THE MINISTER OF STATE OF THE MINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION (SHRI PRAFUL \nPATEL): Sir, I beg to lay on the Table a copy (in English and Hindi) of \nthe Ministry of Civil Aviation Notification No. G.S.R. 21 (E), dated the \n12th January, 2009, publishing the Aircraft (1st Amendment) Rules, 2009, \nunder sub-section (3) of section 14- A of the Aircraft Act, 1934, along \nwith Explanatory Note.  [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10594/09] \nReports and Accounts of various Hotel Corporations (2005-06, 2006-07) \n THE MINISTER OF STATE IN MINISTRY TOURISM AND MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE (SHRIMATI KANTI SINGH): Sir, I beg to lay on the \nTable:- \n I. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers, under \nsub-section (1) of Section 619A of the Companies Act, 1956: \n  (a) Twentieth Annual Report and Accounts of Donyi Polo Ashok \nHotel Corporation Limited, Itanagar, for the year 2006- 2007, \ntogether with the Auditor's Report on the Accounts and the \ncomments of the Comptroller and Auditor General of India \nthereon. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10798/09] \n  (b) Twenty-first Annual Report and Accounts of Pondicherry Ashok \nHotel Corporation Limited, Puducherry, for the year 2006-\n2007, together with the Auditor's Report on the Accounts and \nthe comments of the Comptroller and Auditor General of India \nthereon. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10799/09] \n  (c) Fifth Annual Report and Accounts of Kumarakruppa Frontier \n\n 324 \nHotels Private Limited, New Delhi, for the year 2005 -2006, \ntogether with the Auditor's Report on the Accounts and the \ncomments of the Comptroller and Auditor General of India \nthereon. \n  (d) Reviews by Government on the working of the above \nCorporation. \n\n 325 \n II. Statements each (in English and Hindi) giving reasons for the \ndelay in laying the papers mentioned at (I) above. [Placed in \nLibrary. See No. L.T. 10797/09] \nNotifications of Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas \n THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS \n(SHRI DINSHA J. PATEL): Sir, I beg to lay on the Table:- \n I. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following Notifications \nof the Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas, under Section 62 of \nthe Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board Act, 2006: \n  (1) G.S.R. 800 (E), dated the 19th November, 2008, publishing \nthe Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board (Authorizing \nEntities to Lay, Build, Operate or Expand City or Local \nNatural Gas Distribution Networks) Amendment Regulations, \n2008. \n  (2) G.S.R. 801 (E), dated the 19th November, 2008, publishing \nthe Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board \n(Determination of Network Tariff for city or Local Natural \nGas Distribution Networks and Compression Charge for CNG) \nAmendment Regulations, 2008. \n  (3) G.S.R. 802 (E), dated the 19th November, 2008, publishing \nthe Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board (Authorizing \nEntities to Lay, Build, Operate or Expand Natural Gas \nPipelines) Amendment Regulations, 2008. \n  (4) G.S.R. 807 (E), dated the 20th November, 2008, publishing \nthe Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board \n(Determination of Natural Gas Pipeline Tariff) Regulations, \n2008. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10611/09] \nII. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers: \n (1) Production sharing contract signed between Government of India \n(Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas) and the Reliance \nIndustries Limited for exploration of Coal Bed Methane (CBM) in \nrespect of Block SP (East)-CBM-2001/1. \n (2) Production sharing contract signed between Government of India \n(Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas) and the Reliance \nIndustries Limited for exploration of Coal Bed Methane (CBM) in \nrespect of Block SP (West)-CBM-200/1. [Placed in Library. See No. \nL.T. 10613/09] \n\n 326 \nReports and Accounts of the Bharat Heavy Plates and Vessels Limited, \nVishakhapatnam for 2007-08 and Related Papers \n भार� उद्योग और लोक उद्यम मंत्रालय म� राज्य मंत्री (श्री रघुनाथ झा): महोदय, म� �नम्न�ल�खत \nपत्र सभा पटल पर रखता हूं:- \n I. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers, under \nSub-section (1) of section 619A of the Companies Act, 1956: \n\n 327 \n  (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Bharat Heavy Plate and \nVessels Limited (BHPV), Visakhapatnam, for the year 2007-\n2008, together with the Auditor's Report on the Accounts and \nthe comments of the Comptroller and Auditor General of India \nthereon. \n  (b) Statement by Government accepting the above Report. \n II. Statement (in English and Hindi) giving reasons for the delay in \nlaying the papers mentioned at (I) above. [Placed in Library. See \nNo. L.T. 10610/09] \n_____ \nMESSAGE FROM THE LOK SABHA \nThe Prevention and Control of Infectious and Contagious Diseases  \nin Animals Bill, 2009 \nSECRETARY GENERAL: Sir, I have to report to the House the following \nmessage received from the Lok Sabha, signed by the Secretary- General of \nthe Lok Sabha: \n \"I am directed to inform you that the Prevention and Control of \nInfectious and Contagious Diseases in Animals Bill, 2008, which was \npassed by Rajya Sabha at its sitting held on the 16th December, 2008, \nhas been passed by Lok Sabha at its sitting held on the 20th February, \n2009, with the following amendments:- \nEnacting Formula \n1. Page 2, line 5,- \n For \"Fifty-ninth\", substitute \"Sixtieth\". \nClause-1 \n2. Page 2, line 9,- \n For \"2008\", substitute \"2009\". \n3. I am, therefore, to return herewith the said Bill in accordance \nwith the  \n  provisions of rule 121 of the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of \nBusiness in  \n  Lok Sabha with the request that the concurrence of Rajya Sabha in \nthe said  \n  amendments be communicated to Lok Sabha.\" \nSir, I lay a copy of the Bill on the Table. \n_______ \nREPORT OF THE DEPARTMENT RELATED PARLIAMENTARY STANDING \nCOMMITTEE ON TRANSPORT, TOURISM AND CULTURE \n\n 328 \nSHRI SITARAM YECHURY (West Bengal): Sir, I rise  to present a copy of \nthe One Hundred Forty- ninth Report (in English and Hindi) of the \nDepartment-related Parliamentary Standing Committee on Transport, Tourism \nand Culture on Development of tourism infrastructure and amenities for \nthe Commonwealth Games 2010. \n_______ \n\n 329 \nREPORT OF THE DEPARTMENT RELATED PARLIAMENTARY STANDING \nCOMMITTEE ON PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS \nSHRI TAPAN KUMAR SEN (West Bengal): Sir, I beg to lay on the Table a \ncopy (in English and Hindi) of the Twenty-fifth Report of the Department-\nrelated Parliamentary Standing Committee on Petroleum and Natural Gas \n(2008-2009) on \"Marketing, Supply, Distribution, Dealerships and Pricing \nof Kerosene and other Petroleum Products\". \n______ \nREPORTS OF THE DEPARTMENT RELATED PARLIAMENTARY  \nSTANDING COMMITTEE ON DEFENCE \nSHRIMATI VIPLOVE THAKUR (Himachal Pradesh): Sir, I beg to lay on the \nTable a copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following Reports of the \nDepartment-related Parliamentary Standing Committee on Defence (2008-\n2009):- \n(i) Thirty-fourth Report on \"Human Resource Planning, Shortage of \nManpower, Infusion of Hi- Tech Training and Infrastructure for the \nArmed Forces\"; \n(ii) Thirty-fifth Report on \"Action Taken by the Government on the \nrecommendations of the Committee contained in their Twenty- ninth \nReport (Fourteenth Lok Sabha) on Demands for Grants (2008-2009) of the \nMinistry of Defence\"; and \n(iii) Thirty-sixth Report on \"Status of implementation of Unified \nCommand for Armed Force\". \n______ \nSTATEMENTS BY MINISTERS \nStatus of Implementation of recommendations contained in the Seventy-\nfirst report of the Department Related Parliamentary Standing Committee \non Finance \nTHE MINISTER OF CORPORATE AFFAIRS (SHRI PREM CHAND GUPTA): Sir, I make \na statement regarding status of implementation of recommendations \ncontained in the Seventy- first Report of the Department- related \nParliamentary Standing Committee on Finance. \nStatus of Implementation of recommendations contained in the Twenty-sixth \nreport  \nof the Department Related Parliamentary Standing Committee on Personnel,  \n\n 330 \nPublic Grievances and Law and Justice \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF LAW AND JUSTICE (SHRI K. \nVENKATAPATHY): Sir, I make a statement regarding status of implementation \nof recommendations contained in the Twenty- sixth Report of the \nDepartment-related Parliamentary Standing Committee on Personnel, Public \nGrievances and Law and Justice. \n______ \n\n 331 \nMATTERS RAISED WITH PERMISSION \nProblems being faced by paddy farmers of Jharkhand in selling their crops \nto F.C.I. \nश्री यशवंत �सन्हा (झारखंड): उपसभाप�त महोदय, म� जो मामला उठाने जा रहा हूं, वह अखबार \nक� खबर पर आधा�रत नह�ं है, बिल्क जो व्यिक्तगत अनुभव हुआ है, उस पर आधा�रत है। म� 31 \nजनवर� को अपने िजले हजार�बाग म� एक स्थान से दूसरे स्थान पर जा रहा था। उसी दरम्यान वहां के \n�कसान� ने हमको रोका और यह कहा �क यहां जो Food Corporation of India का धान �बक्र�-\nक्रय के न् द्र है, उसम� धान क� खर�द नह�ं हो रह� है। जब म� उस क्रय के न् द्र पर गया तो म�ने दे खा �क \nव � क� ग डे होने बावजूद साढ़े ग्यारह बजे �दन म� वहां एक बड़ा ताला लटका हुआ था और उस क्रय के न् द्र \nपर कोई पदा�धकार� नह�ं था। यह क्रय के न् द्र Grand Trunk Road पर िस्थत है। आपको यह सुनकर \nआश्चयर् होगा �क वहां पर धान से भरे हजार� बोरे पड़े थे और उन बोर� पर आस-पास के �कसान ब ै ठे \nहुए थे। जब म� वहां पर पहुंचा तो उन �कसान� ने हमसे यह� कहा �क साहब, हम लोग 10-12 �दन से \nयहां खुले आसमान के नीचे इन्ह�ं बोर� पर सोने के �लए बाध्य हो रहे ह�, ले�कन यह धान हमसे खर�दा \nनह�ं जा रहा है। जब म�ने और जानकार� हा�सल क�, तो पता चला �क यह पूरा �सस्टम ह� �बचौ�लय� \nके हाथ म� है। �बचौ�लए गांव म� जाते ह� और �कसान� से कहते ह� �क यह Food Corporation of \nIndia तुम्हारा धान नह�ं खर�दे गी, इस�लए तुम सस्ती क�मत पर हमको धान बेच दो। �कसान पांच सौ \nरुपए प्र�त िक्वंटल के आस-पास धान बेचने को मजबूर हो रहे ह� और Food Corporation of \nIndia रात के अंधेरे म� उन्ह�ं �बचौ�लए से उसी धान को 930 रुपए प्र�त िक्वंटल के �हसाब से खर�द \nरह� है। \nमहोदय, लोग� ने कहा �क Food Corporation of India के  जो officials ह�, वे कभी \nभी क्रय के न् द्र पर नह�ं आए ह�। उन्ह�ने इस बात क� कोई �च ंत ा नह�ं क� �क क्रय के न् द्र पर धान खर�दा \nजा रहा है या नह�ं खर�दा जा रहा है। म� वहां पर बैठ गया और म�ने कहा �क Food Corporation \nof India के पदा�धका�रय� को खबर करो। उ स के बाद Food Corporation of India के  जो \nपदा�धकार� थे, जो लोकल सब�ड�वजनल मिजस्ट्रेट थे, ये लोग वहां पर आए। Food Corporation \nof India के पदा�धकार� ने हमसे कहा �क हमारे गोदाम म� जगह नह�ं है, हमारे पास ट्रक नह�ं है \nऔर हमारे पास बोरे नह�ं ह� �क हम धान का क्रय कर�। जब म�ने यह कहा �क म� यहां से तब तक नह�ं \nउठूं गा, जब तक �क यहां पर धान का क्रय शुरू नह�ं हो जाता है। इ स के बाद SDO के intervene \nकरने पर बोरा भी आ गया, ट्रक भी आ गया और गोदाम म� जगह भी हो गई और धान का क्रय चालू \nहो गया। \nमहोदय, एक �कसान ने कहा �क साहब, यहां पर खुलेआम भ्रष्टाचार है। Food Corporation \nof India के officials खुलेआम पैसा मांगते ह� �क तुम हमको इतना पैसा दो, तब हम तुम्हारा \nधान खर�द�गे। म�ने उसको कहा �क तुम इस बात का �ल�खत रूप म� �शकायत करो, तो उसने �ल�खत \nरूप म�\n �शकायत रखी। म�ने उसको endorse करक े वहां के officer-in-charge को दे �दया। ये \nसार� धांध�लयां वहां चल रह� ह�। यह कोई एक क्रय के न् द्र का सवाल नह�ं है। \nमहोदय, पूरे झारखंड म� �कसान� के साथ यह� अन्याय हो रहा है और कह�ं भी �कसान� से सह� दाम \n\n 332 \nपर अनाज नह�ं खर�दा जा रहा है। म� सरकार का ध्यान आकृ ष्ट करता हूं �क वह तत्काल इसम� हस्त�ेप \nकरे और यह सु�निश्चत करे �क सरकार क� नी�त के अनुसार वहां पर �कसान� से धान खर�दा जा रहा \nहै। धन्यवाद। \nश्री एस.एस. अहलुवा�लया (झारखंड): महोदय, म� इस �वषय से अपने आपको संबद्ध करता हूं। \n\n 333 \nश्री प्रभात झा (मध्य प्रदे श): महोदय, म� इस �वषय से अपने आपको संबद्ध करता हूं। \nश्री प्रकाश जावडेकर (महाराष्ट्र): महोदय, म� इस �वषय से अपने आपको संबद्ध करता हूं। \nडा. �ान प्रकाश �पला�नया (राजस्थान): महोदय, म� इस �वषय से अपने आपको संबद्ध करता हूं। \nTerrorist and smuggling activities along Indo-Myanmar border \nश्री प्रकाश जावडेकर (महाराष्ट्र): उपसभाप�त महोदय, सुर�ा दे श क� सबसे प्रमुख �च ंत ा होनी \nचा�हए। सरकार दावे तो कर रह� है �क हम सुर�ा के �लए पूरे चौकसबंद ह�। आज तक िजस �वषय पर \nध्यान नह�ं गया है, म� उसी �वषय पर ध्यान �दलाने के �लए इसे शून्य-काल म� उपिस्थत कर रहा हूं। \nम्यांमार क� सीमा का मुद्दा है। �पछले मह�ने म�णपुर म� सेना के एक क� प, जहां कमाण्डोज रहते ह�, पर \nहमला हुआ। वहां पर बम �वस्फोट हुआ और उसको उड़ा �दया गया। हमला करने के बाद हमलावर तीन \nघंटे म� म्यांमार भाग गए। इस प्रकार हमला करक े म्यांमार म� जाना और वहां पर शरण लेना, यह नॉथर्-\nईस्ट के �लए आम बात हो गई है। हम बंगला दे श क� सीमा के बारे म� बोलते ह�, चीन क� सीमा के \nबारे म� बोलते ह�, पा�कस्तान से सट� सीमा के बारे म� बोलते ह�, ले�कन सदन म� म्यांमार से सट� जो \nसीमा है, जो पूव�त्तर के चार राज्य� - अरुणाचल, नागालैण्ड, �मजोरम और म�णपुर से सट� हजार� \n�कलोमीटर क� सीमा है, उ स के बारे म� बहुत कम बार बोलते ह�। आज जो arms smuggling हो रहा \nहै। नॉथर्-ईस्ट के insurgents को जो arms �मल रहे ह�, वे सारे arms चीन के होते ह�। जहां भी \nछापे मारे गए ह�, वहां चीन के arms पाए गए ह�। चीन के arms चीन से वाया म्यांमार यहां आ रहे \nह�। तो अरुणाचल, नागाल�ड, �मजोरम और म�णपुर - इन चार राज्य� से जुड़े ह�। आतंकवाद� वारदात� \nइधर हो रह� ह�, लोग तुरं त भागकर वहां जा रहे ह�। उनक े �खलाफ कोई कायर्वाह� नह�ं हो रह� है। वहां \nआतंकवाद� प्र�श�ण �श�वर भी ह�। नारको�टक्स का 