 यह अब आ गई है, हमारा भला करे गी, तब और �कसी से उम्मीद नह�ं \nहोती। आपने �पछले दो-तीन साल� म� �दल्ल� वाल� के �लए बहुत कु छ �कया है और आज एक समय है \nजब आपने उनक े �दल�  को  छू ने क� को�शश क� है। लोग तड़पे ह�, आंसुओं से रोये ह�, यह हमार� \nवजह से नह�ं बिल्क कोटर् क�  \n\n 459 \nवजह से हुआ है। आपने बड़े अ च् छे कदम उठाये ह� और आज वक्त है �क हम उनक� और मदद कर�। म� \nपुरजोर त र � के से इस �बल का समथर्न करता हूं। \nSHRI PRASANTA CHATTERJEE (WEST BENGAL): Sir, the situation of Delhi, \nwhich resulted in the enactment of this Bill, was very grave. In the \npresent scenario, we have no option but to support the Bill. But, Sir, I \nwould like to tell that this is the problem of all the major metropolitan \ncities. Look at the situation of Mumbai. We had our situation even in \nKolkata also. The question is how to stop continuous influx of rural \npopulation to the urban areas in the present economic scenario, political \nand socio-economic factors. Otherwise, in every metropolitan city, this \nwill happen, particularly in the present international economic situation \nwhen the people are coming back from other countries. And, the problem of \nurban areas cannot be fought in isolation. It has relation with the \nproblems of rural areas and we have to see how to stop this continuous \ninflux from rural areas. It is not that one hospital is built, or good \nroads are built in rural areas; that should be done. But, Sir, the main \nthrust has to be given on land reforms, providing the land to the tiller \nto improve the rural economy. What steps will you take, what steps will \nthe country take in this direction? If you do not find an answer from \nthis point of view, the problem of this continuous influx cannot be dealt \nwith. We know in 1969 to 1975, in West Bengal, how we faced this \nsituation. Here, in Delhi, if you want to solve this problem, we have to \nthink as to how we see the position in UP., in Rajasthan, or in M.P. What \nis our answer? Farmers of Rajasthan wanted water, and instead of getting \nwater, they received bullets. If this is our answer to this question, \nthen, you cannot stop this problem. That is the major issue, to which we \nhave to find an answer. Have we fought for the land to the tillers? Have \nwe really fought for the land reforms? Sir, we know that many of us here \ncome from very wealthy families, from landlord background. These are the \nreal questions. You cannot ignore this question. But, so far as this \nMaster Plan of Delhi is concerned, there are serious violations. I \nattended the PAC meeting. The commercial complexes have been built up in \nthe residential areas. Schools and colleges have been built up in the \nresidential areas and the conditions have been violated continuously. So, \nthese things will have to be administratively looked into. \nSir, while saying that we have no objection to this, I would also say \n\n 460 \nthat to deal with these problems, the Government should look into the \nproblems of the small business houses, housing for the poor. If the BPL \nfamilies do not get housing free of cost, where will they stay. \nDefinitely, they will stay in the jhompris. These are some of the \nquestions. \nWith these few words, I again say that we have no option but to \nsupport this Bill. I demand the Ministry that they should be brought to \nprotect the Master Plan. On the one hand, you continue to see the \nviolation of the Master Plan, and, on the other, you come to make these \nprovisions. These things will not work. Thank you. \nश्री र�व शंकर प्रसाद: माननीय उपसभाप�त जी, सबसे पहले आपने जो मुझे इस महत्वपूणर् �बल पर \nअपने �वचार रखने का अवसर �दया है, म� उ स के �लए कृ त� हूं। \n\n 461 \n म� माननीय मंत्री, श्री अजय माकन जी और हमारे बड़े अ च् छे �मत्र और व�रष्ठ नेता, श्री जय \nप्रकाश अग्रवाल जी के सामने एक सांसद के रूप म�, एक कानून के जानकार के रूप म� कु छ गंभीर \nसमस्याओं को रखना चाहता हूं। \nमहोदय, म� कहना चाहता हूं �क यह एक्ट आप तीसर� बार ला रहे ह�। पहल� बार आप \nordinance लाए, उ स के बाद 